  "notes": {
    "cmsgpack": "Standard MessagePack as produced by Redis Lua cmsgpack.pack: strings use the str family (never bin), integers use the smallest unsigned int family member, booleans are 0xc2/0xc3. See 22-location-store-redis.md#7.",
    "jsonByteLayering": "jsonBytesHex is the exact canonical JSON encoded as UTF-8 bytes; it is the rawBytes input consumed verbatim by the cmsgpack layer. Consumers field-compare \"decoded\" against their own JSON encoder output, then take jsonBytesHex verbatim and cmsgpack-encode it to byte-compare against cmsgpackMemberHex/fullValueHex. JSON field order is not significant for the field-compare step even though the byte-compare step pins one exact serialization.",
    "payloadEncoding": "The authority record's payload field is base64 inside JSON, per 21-location-runtime.md#2.4. As of the spec revision that added this fixture, the cpp provider still encodes this field as hex internally; that is a C-4 conversion item, not part of this fixture.",
    "objectGeneration": "authorityActorJson/authoritySpotJson.objectGeneration is issued from a Store-wide monotonic sequence, not a per-identity counter (checklist C-2b).",
    "capacityBundle": "allocation.capacity is {actors, spots, spotType}, matching dotnet ZLinkCapacityVector/ZLinkPlacementAllocation and node's in-memory authority test fixtures field-for-field. spotType is null for actor allocations; for spot allocations it carries {objectKind, stableType, count} per 21-location-runtime.md#2.3 (\"Spot slot 1과 해당 Spot 종류·stable type slot 1\") -- a flat slot counter cannot express which (spotKind, stableType) pair was reserved.",
    "hashtagRationale": "The zlink-location-v3 and zlink-relocation-v1 domain tags are wrapped in Redis Cluster hashtag braces ({...}) in every assembled key. This forces the whole opaque-record domain (and the whole relocation-blob domain) onto one hash slot by design, so a multi-key EVAL script (record + sequence counter + index, per 22-location-store-redis.md#7) stays same-slot atomic under Redis Cluster; a brace-less key would let Cluster route the keys to different slots and break that atomicity.",
    "descriptorFieldInventory": "meshNodeDescriptor/clientServerDescriptor/fanoutPublisherDescriptor \"descriptor\" content is the FULL normative field set derived from 21-location-runtime.md#2.3/#3 plus the spec glossary's own .NET code blocks (ZLinkMeshNodeDescriptor, ZLinkClientServerServerDescriptor, ZLinkFanoutPublisherDescriptor, 01-glossary.md) and cross-checked against cpp/java/dotnet/node source. A provider-internal \"generation\" field some in-progress language implementations attach to this envelope is deliberately excluded here: the opaque record's own cmsgpack \"version\" member (this fixture's top-level \"version\" field on each value vector) already is the storage-row CAS generation, so a second copy inside the JSON would be redundant -- this mirrors dotnet's design, which keeps the storage-row generation out of the descriptor record entirely."
  }
